From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 49/49] PC5: a large overlay, and Wine's own Direct3D on Vulkan for a
 game ([debug] env WINE_D3D_CONFIG)

The overlay's lines (PW_PC5_HUD_*) take a flag, PW_PC5_HUD_LARGE: up to
two lines at a time, each its value in glyphs twice the size over its
label, the next two every 3 seconds when more are on. The overlay is
VideoOut's 64x64 hardware cursor, so its lines were 5x7 glyphs and hard
to read on a TV; the large overlay keeps that image and its cost. The
memory shows the gigabytes used ("5.1G"). PwPc5HudStats counts the
updates (seconds), and libvulkan.prx keeps the flag and counts them.

A profile's [debug] env takes WINE_D3D_CONFIG, so PC5 can set Wine's
own Direct3D (wined3d) to draw with Vulkan instead of OpenGL for a game
whose Direct3D is set to Wine's (renderer=vulkan).
